$ cadence help projects
exit 0
--- requests
--- stdout
usage: cadence projects <verb> [flags]

Verbs:
  adopt      Adopt a registry version into the project by reference
             --project PROJECT --if-match IF_MATCH [--dry-run] --body JSON
  archive    Archive a project (soft; reversible)
             --project PROJECT --if-match IF_MATCH [--dry-run]
  edit       Change a project's name, description, locales, domain, base model or budgets
             --project PROJECT --if-match IF_MATCH [--dry-run] --body JSON
  get        Get a project
             --project PROJECT
  list       List projects
             [--archived]
  new        Create a project from the wizard's choices and bootstrap its repository (202 with the bootstrap job)
             [--dry-run] --body JSON
  note       Append a dated learning to the project's NOTES.md and commit it to main
             --project PROJECT --if-match IF_MATCH [--dry-run] --body JSON
  search     Search entities of this project and the registry with free text and qualifiers
             --project PROJECT [--q Q] [--limit N]
  sync       Diff the project against Cadence's current templates and skills and offer the update as a draft branch
             --project PROJECT --if-match IF_MATCH [--dry-run]

`cadence projects <verb> --help` describes one verb's flags and body.
--- stderr
